# NOTES
# 1. RBMK turbines: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turboatom explicitly names Leningrad, Kursk, and Smolensk NPPs as recipients of Turboatom's (Kharkiv Turbine Plant) 500 MW turbines in the early 1970s, and separately names Rostov NPP as a recipient of Turboatom's 1000 MW turbines (1982-85). This directly contradicts the heuristic's blanket "Power Machines (LMZ)" default for every plant/unit in the batch except the newest VVER-1200/TOI builds (Kursk II, confirmed Power Machines PJSC via en.wikipedia.org Kursk NPP). Reading: Turboatom (Ukraine, Kharkiv) supplied essentially all Soviet-era RBMK and early VVER-1000 turbines; Power Machines (Russia, ex-LMZ) only became the default supplier for new domestic builds after Ukrainian supply became politically unavailable (~2014). This pattern was extended by analogy (MED confidence) to Leningrad II and Novovoronezh II turbines.
# 2. Architect-engineer: the regional "Atomenergoproekt" institutes are indeed distinct organizations, as the task brief warned. ru.wikipedia.org's Rostov NPP article directly attributes the plant's technical design to the Gorky (Nizhny Novgorod) branch of Teploelektroproekt, now branded "AO ASE" — not the Moscow Atomenergoproekt used (per direct source) at Kursk I. Because Rosatom's domestic VVER-1200 "AES-2006" new-build program (Novovoronezh II, Leningrad II, Kursk II) is documented industry-wide as executed by this same Nizhny Novgorod/ASE lineage, the Moscow-Atomenergoproekt default was marked WRONG for all of those plants (MED confidence, analogized rather than plant-by-plant sourced).
# 3. Constructor: "Minsredmash" is a ministry, not a company, per the task brief. A sourced successor construction organization was only found for Kursk ("Kurskatomenergostroy," per en.wikipedia.org). No equivalent named entity was found for Leningrad, Smolensk, or Novovoronezh 1 in available sources — these were left UNVERIFIABLE rather than assuming a parallel "Leningradatomenergostroy" / "Smolenskatomenergostroy" name without a citation.
# 4. RPV manufacturer: "None" is CONFIRMED (HIGH) for every RBMK unit — channel-type reactors have no single reactor pressure vessel. Izhora Plants is CONFIRMED (HIGH) for the original Novovoronezh station (all 5 units), directly sourced. Atommash (Volgodonsk) is CONFIRMED as the correct value for Rostov (contradicting the Izhora default), matching the task brief's note that Atommash fabricated later VVER-1000 vessels. For the newest VVER-1200 builds (Leningrad II, Kursk II, Novovoronezh II) neither Izhora nor Atommash could be confirmed on a plant-specific basis — both are documented as active VVER-1200-class vessel suppliers in the same era (Izhora: Akademik Lomonosov, Akkuyu unit 2, 2020s), so these were left UNVERIFIABLE.
# 5. Kursk 2 unit 3 (Under Construction) has no heuristic-guessed values in the input (all four fields already "None") — excluded from verification entirely, no output rows generated for it.
